Error [jet.ReadOnlyValueNotOwned]: This loop can't take handles out of a field or index
  --> tests/ui/loop_task_list_index.jet:4:21
    |
  4 |     loop h in groups[0] -> total += h.join() ?? 0
    |                     ^^^
 Why: Each step hands you the handle itself, and a task handle cannot be copied — so the loop takes the whole list
 Fix: Bind the list into a local this scope owns first (`hs := …`), then write `loop h in hs { … }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0120

Error [jet.SingleUseDropped]: `groups` still owes `consume`
  --> tests/ui/loop_task_list_index.jet:2:5
    |
  2 |     groups: [[task 1, task 2]]
    |     ^^^^^^
 Why: This value's type is `#SingleUse`, so it carries a job that has to be done — dropping it without doing that job leaves the work undone (an unjoined task, an unreleased lock)
 Fix: Consume it exactly once: pass it to a `&&` parameter, or `return` it — or write `#Unsafe("reason") { consume(groups) }` to discard it deliberately
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0140
